{
 "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/pro-menu-bar-walk",
 "seed": "The menu bar reads like a professional Mac editor's, at Next defaults with no flag changed. On a picture it runs File, Edit, Image, Layer, Measure, View, Window, Help: no Video menu of rows left over from the retired recording window, Capture folded into File the way Preview files Take Screenshot, and Show History in Window. On a video, Clip and Sequence arrive between Layer and Measure, split the way Final Cut and Premiere split them. On both, no two live rows print the same shortcut. It needs the probe in front, because a menu bar only reads live for the app that has focus.",
